just check               # tests, config, readiness, evaluations and the platform's doctor
just ask "How many days of annual leave do I get?"
```

## Where things are

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `rag.yaml` | Which component fills each slot; includes the platform's profiles and says only what differs |
| `src/{{ module }}/components.py` | This project's own components (registered through an entry point) |
| `corpus/sample/` | Sample documents: replace them with yours |
| `eval/questions.yaml` | Labelled questions: search, answers, abstention, access control |
| `eval/guards.yaml` | Guardrail cases: attacks AND ordinary questions |
| `retention.yaml` | How long indexed documents may stay; legal holds |
| `docs/cards/system-{{ slug }}.md` | The system card (fill it in before production) |
| `docs/risk-acceptance.md` | What is specific to this project in the platform's risk register |
| `docs/adr/` | Decisions, starting with building on the platform |
| `Dockerfile`, `deploy/` | The platform's image plus this project; the platform's prod overlay in `rag-{{ slug }}` |

## How to change things

- **Switch a component:** one line in `rag.yaml`, e.g. `reranker: none` or
  `pipeline: {use: corrective}`. `uv run rag components` lists every option.
- **Add your own component:** register it in `src/{{ module }}/components.py`, name it in `rag.yaml`.
- **Use your documents:** put them in `corpus/`, list them in `eval/questions.yaml` with real
  questions from users, and raise the thresholds in the `justfile` as the set grows.
- **Take platform improvements:** `uvx copier update` (template) and a new `rag-core` 1.x
  (`uv lock --upgrade-package rag-core`); both arrive as a reviewed pull request.

The platform's standards, which `rag doctor` checks: `docs/standards/rag-standards.md` in the
platform repository.
